# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.uv/
# Coverage (surfaced in CI as a job summary + artifact; never committed)
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/

# Docs site build (mkdocs) + local docs venv
/site/
.docs-venv/

# Data
.DS_Store
demo/data/
demo/out/

# Secrets / credentials — never commit (see SECURITY.md)
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.pypirc
credentials
credentials.*
*.credentials
secrets.*

# Maintainer-local competitive review (issue #189): candid competitor/gap notes that
# were never intended to ship on a public repo or docs site. Kept on disk, out of git.
docs/COMPETITIVE-GAP-ANALYSIS.md
# Maintainer-internal operating material dropped from the shipping tree for the same reason:
# a go-live checklist, the provenance memos naming the private predecessor repos and costing
# their reinvention, deck speaker notes, and a per-PR review whose asks have all shipped.
# Restore a local copy with `git show <ref>:<path>` if you need one; it stays out of git.
docs/GO-LIVE-RUNBOOK.md
docs/PORTING-MAP.md
docs/ASSET-INVENTORY.md
docs/PITCH-SLIDES.md
docs/audits/
benchmark/enterprise-gold/store/
# official eval data: dataset-derived artifacts stay local (HotpotQA CC BY-SA share-alike);
# judgments/maps/results are committed as dated records. The scripts that wrote the ignored
# files below were removed with the retrieval layer on 2026-11-10, so nothing in the tree
# regenerates them; the patterns stay so an old local copy is never committed.
benchmark/official-data/*/export/
benchmark/official-data/*/*-dev.jsonl
benchmark/official-data/*/*-test.jsonl
benchmark/official-data/*/query-surfaces.jsonl
benchmark/official-data/*/calibration-sample.jsonl
# e2e-sota-run campaign corpus (S1): raw acquisitions + downloaded archives stay local —
# every dataset lane keeps its corpus on the machine that fetched it
# (see latence_benchmark/campaign/corpus_stage.py CORPUS_PLAN).
benchmark/sota-corpus/*/raw/
benchmark/sota-corpus/**/*.zip
# S2: extracted PDFs + OCR'd markdown inherit each dataset's lane — derived data stays
# local, never committed (s2-ocr ticket constraint).
benchmark/sota-corpus/*/pdfs/
benchmark/sota-corpus/*/markdown/
# S2 gate artifacts under the campaign root hold corpus-derived page images/markdown.
benchmark/sota-campaign/stages/s2-ocr/spot-check/
benchmark/sota-campaign/stages/s2-ocr/pod-metrics.json
benchmark/sota-campaign/stages/s2-ocr/failures.jsonl
benchmark/sota-corpus/s2-output/
benchmark/sota-corpus/s3-exports/
# S3 gate artifacts derived from research-only / share-alike datasets (OHR-Bench,
# ViDoSeek, UDA, 2Wiki, MultiHop-RAG): the Quality Reports carry induced type names
# lifted from the source text and the chunk samples carry raw passages. Aggregate
# metrics (stages/s3-pipeline/metrics.json) and the pipeline configs ARE committed.
benchmark/sota-campaign/stages/s3-pipeline/reports/
benchmark/sota-campaign/stages/s3-pipeline/chunk-validation/samples/
benchmark/sota-campaign/stages/s3-pipeline/chunk-validation/induction-sample.jsonl
# Local S3 export copies (corpus-derived text + embeddings — same lanes as above) and
# run logs; the committed evidence is metrics.json + the stage REPORTs, never raw runs.
benchmark/sota-campaign/stages/s3-pipeline/exports/
benchmark/sota-campaign/stages/*.log
benchmark/sota-campaign/stages/s3-pipeline/chunk-validation/*.log
# The whole acquired-corpus tree is dataset-derived and stays local (per-dataset lanes in
# latence_benchmark.campaign.corpus_stage.CORPUS_PLAN; nothing under it is tracked).
benchmark/sota-corpus/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private operating material (ticket 05 Part B — public-repo scrub)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These files stay ON DISK and keep working for the maintainer; they are simply
# not part of the published repository. Each is a record of how this codebase was
# operated rather than something a reader can use.
#
# Hostile-audit findings ledgers: per-file historical vulnerabilities with
# reproduction steps and adjudications, addressed to whoever ran the audit.
issues/audit/
issues/audit-arch/
# Campaign execution logs (wave reports) and the out-of-scope "logged, not
# chased" ledger. Their durable content is restated in the ADRs and NN-report.md.
issues/wayfinder-*/waves/
issues/**/FINDINGS.md
issues/wayfinder-enterprise-serving/architecture-pass.md
# Personal WIP pointer, internal issue-ID cross-reference, launch plan.
issues/NEXT.md
issues/GITHUB-MAP.md
issues/RELEASE-FLEET.md
# This scrub's own audit: it necessarily quotes the identifiers it removed.
issues/wayfinder-enterprise-serving/tickets/05-part-b-inventory.md
# Part A of the same pass: an editorial rating of five named third-party projects that
# also tabulates two external maintainers' email addresses. Same grounds as Part B.
issues/wayfinder-enterprise-serving/tickets/05-part-a-comparison.md
# Local experiment traces from the same tree (their own .gitignore went with the
# roadmap condensation, so the rule has to live here to keep them unpublishable).
issues/wayfinder-enterprise-serving/tickets/06-graph-inertia/traces/
# Maintainer-local assistant tooling.
.claude/
# Build-harness scripts: they drive a maintainer-local agent harness, hardcode a
# commit-author identity and a `git push origin main`, and no test covers them.
orchestration/
# One operator's campaign run: live config (pod endpoint, budget cap) and run
# state. `latence-campaign init` regenerates campaign.yaml for anyone else, and
# STATE.json is rewritten on every stage transition. No test reads either.
benchmark/sota-campaign/campaign.yaml
benchmark/sota-campaign/STATE.json
# Decision memo addressed to the maintainer in second person (names a personal account and
# PyPI identity). Kept on disk; never published. ADR-0062 is the public decision record.
issues/05-decisions.local.md
# Internal session status report (names the maintainer, another session's in-flight files, and
# gitignored FINDINGS). Kept on disk; the measured evidence it summarises is published separately.
issues/04-enterprise-readiness.local.md
